Rule 1 (torch.equal input tensors must have the same size and elements)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= shape(v_1) = shape(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (torch.equal input tensors must have compatible dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (torch.equal should not be used with string tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 12
>>
Rule 4 (torch.equal tensors must have at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 5 (torch.equal input tensors can have boolean dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 0) ∧ (dtype_(v_2) = 0)
>>
Rule 6 (if one tensor is empty, the other must also be empty)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 0) ∨ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 7 (torch.equal tensors cannot be both scalars if their values are different)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 0 then v_1 = v_2
>>
Rule 8 (If one tensor is boolean, the other should also be boolean)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = 0) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 0)
